[ti:Day 08]

[00:00.00]momentum [məˈmentəm]n. 动力，冲力；势头；动量 例 He needs momentum and efforts to realise his targets. 搭 gain momentum 发展加快；势头增大 / keep the good momentum 保持良好势头 / momentum balance 动量守恒
[00:17.52]intervene [ˌɪntəˈviːn]vi. 干涉，干预；调停；介入 例 The market economy can only function if the state intervenes.
[00:28.08]assent [əˈsent]v. 赞成，同意 n. 赞同；财产转让证书 例 His assent to the proposal clinched the bargain. 搭 assent to 赞同 / with one assent 一致同意地
[00:40.56]mercantile [ˈmɜːkəntaɪl]a. 商人的；商业的
[00:44.40]bundle [ˈbʌndl]n. 捆(或包、扎)在一起的东西 vt. 捆，束 例 He was burdened with a large bundle of magazines. 搭 bundle up 把…捆起来
[00:55.32]segregate [ˈseɡrɪɡeɪt]v. (使)分开；(使)隔离 例 The device is used to segregate hazardous waste.
[01:04.44]panic [ˈpænɪk]n. 惊慌；财政恐慌 v. (使)恐慌 a. 恐慌 的；恐慌引起的 例 The rumour is panicing many citizens into buying edible salt. 搭 get into a panic 陷入恐慌之中 / panic button 紧急保险按钮；应急开关
[01:20.76]identity [aɪˈdentəti]n. 身份；个性，特性；同一性，一致 性 例 To implement this requirement, you should properly configure the authentication of a user identity. 搭 identity card 身份证 / identity certificate 身 份证明书 / identity crisis 身份危机
[01:42.96]outstrip [ˌaʊtˈstrɪp]vt. 超越；胜过 例 In America, the tuition increase outstrips inflation by four percentage points annually. We divide our sales team into a direct sales force and an inside sales force.
[02:03.24]guilder [ˈɡɪldə(r)]n. 盾(荷兰货币单位) 例 The Dutch guilder was retired in 2002 when it was replaced by the Euro.
[02:13.80]community [kəˈmjuːnəti]n. 社区，社会；团体，界；(动植物 的)群落 例 The conference will make further efforts to enlist the support of the international community for their just struggle. 搭 community diversity 群落多样性
[02:34.08]perishable [ˈperɪʃəbl]a. 易腐败的 n. [常pl.]易腐食品
[02:38.76]transact [trænˈzækt]v. 办理，处理；交易；商议
[02:42.60]camaraderie [ˌkæməˈrɑːdəri]n. (战友、同学间的)情谊 例 This time, a stronger and more confident China is sending messages of conciliation and camaraderie.
[02:57.60]infuse [ɪnˈfjuːz]vt. 灌输；使充满；把…注入；沏(茶)， 泡(草药) vi. 浸，泡 例 The corporation may lose the opportunity to infuse flexibility into the IT portfolio. 搭 infuse with 灌输
[03:13.68]numismatic [ˌnjuːmɪzˈmætɪk]a. 钱币的；钱币学的；奖章的
[03:18.48]ledger [ˈledʒə(r)]n. 分类账；底账；总账；账簿
[03:22.20]countersign [ˈkaʊntəsaɪn]vt. 副署；会签 例 You will receive our S/C and please countersign and return one copy to us for file.
[03:34.32]potential [pəˈtenʃl]a. 可能的；潜在的；有潜力的 n. 潜 力，潜能；可能性
[03:39.60]undercut [ˈʌndəkʌt]vt. 廉价出售；削价；削减，削弱 例 The policy undercut farming operations, and prevented farmers from receiving the real value of their commodities.
[03:55.56]quittance [ˈkwɪtəns]n. 免除(债务或义务等的)证书；收据； 赔偿；补偿 例 Omittance is no quittance.
[04:03.60]wrongfully [ˈrɒŋfəli]ad. 不正当地；不妥地 例 He is wrongfully dismissed.
[04:10.32]overtrading [ˌəʊvəˈtreɪdɪŋ]n. 过量交易；超资力经营
[04:14.88]dominate [ˈdɒmɪneɪt]vt. 在…中占首要地位；支配；占优势 vi. 处于支配地位；拥有优势 例 No nation should try to dominate another nation. 搭 dominate over 在…方面占据支配地位
[04:28.80]foreground [ˈfɔːɡraʊnd]n. 前景；突出的地方；最显著的位 置 例 It's great to see this large technology company at the foreground of the trend. 搭 foreground camera 前景摄像机 / foreground job 前台作业
[04:46.32]external [ɪkˈstɜːnl]a. 外部的；外表的；对外的；外来的
[04:50.64]flier [ˈflaɪə(r)]n. 冒险买卖，投机买卖；(广告)传单； 证券市场投机者；飞行员 例 Someone gave me this advertising flier at the entrance. 搭 take a flier 冒险，贸然尝试
[05:04.08]utility [juːˈtɪləti]n. 效用；实用；公用事业 a. 实用型 的；经济型的 搭 utility room 杂品储藏室
[05:11.16]bridging [ˈbrɪdʒɪŋ]n. 桥接，跨接 a. 过渡性的；临时的 例 Hindi is the national language of the country, whereas English is the bridging language that will give you an indication of community.
[05:29.04]negotiable [nɪˈɡəʊʃiəbl]a. 可谈判的，可磋商的；(票据、证 券等)可转让的，可流通的，可议付的 例 The prices of the commodity are negotiable for quantity purchases.
[05:42.84]dismantle [dɪsˈmæntl]vt. 拆开，拆卸；废除，取消
[05:46.92]snip [snɪp]n. 一定会成功的事；不吃亏的买卖；便宜 货 例 This computer is a snip at ￥2,000.
[05:54.00]readily [ˈredɪli]ad. 乐意地；无困难地，容易地
[05:57.72]overtly [əʊˈvɜːtli]ad. 明显地；公开地 例 The director has overtly announced his support for technical innovation.
[06:08.76]risk-averse [ˈrɪskəvɜːs]a. 不愿承担风险的
[06:12.60]impart [ɪmˈpɑːt]vt. 给予；传授；告知，透露 例 I really have no secret about business to impart to you.
[06:21.72]scanty [ˈskænti]a. 不足的；贫乏的；勉强够的；将近的 搭 be scanty of 缺乏 / scanty crop 歉收
[06:28.80]gratuity [ɡrəˈtjuːəti]n. 抚恤金，养老金；小费；赏金 例 The tipping problem in many European countries is solved by automatically adding a 15 percent gratuity to the bill.
[06:44.88]resell [ˌriːˈsel]vt. 再卖；转售，转卖(财产等) 例 I find it difficult to resell shares of the company.
[06:54.00]payoff [ˈpeɪɒf]n. 报酬；盈利；发工资；结算 a. 支付 的；决定性的；产生结果的
[06:59.28]colleague [ˈkɒliːɡ]n. 同事，同僚 例 Every colleague has the right to express his own opinion.
[07:08.16]optimum [ˈɒptɪməm]a. 最合适的；最优的，最佳的 n. 最 大限度；最优效果；最佳条件
[07:13.80]promissory [ˈprɒmɪsəri]a. 允诺的；约定的；有约束力的；约 定支付的；使保险契约生效之特约条款的
[07:20.64]secondment [sɪˈkɒndmənt]n. 暂借，借调 例 She was sent to the sales department on secondment. 搭 on secondment 借调
[07:31.32]concession [kənˈseʃn]n. 特许，特许权；佣金；租地营业商 摊；让步，妥协；承认 例 I am prepared to make some concessions on minor details, but I cannot compromise on fundamentals. 搭 make a concession to sb. 向某人让步
[07:50.04]bourse [bʊəs]n. 交易所；证券交易所 例 The NYSE management team has a strong incentive to push for the Deutsche Bourse deal.
[08:01.44]depot [ˈdepəʊ]n. 仓库；车库
[08:03.84]debit [ˈdebɪt]vt. 把…记入借方；借记 例 The new policy offers the additional options to pay online with a debit card.
[08:14.64]equity [ˈekwəti]n. 公平；抵押资产净值；[pl.] (公司的) 普通股；股本 例 The equity-based earnings rose a lot.
[08:23.76]unacceptable [ˌʌnəkˈseptəbl]a. 无法接受的；不受欢迎的；不 能令人满意的
[08:29.52]setback [ˈsetbæk]n. 挫折；阻碍；衰退
[08:32.64]stagnant [ˈstæɡnənt]a. 停滞的；萧条的
[08:36.00]constantly [ˈkɒnstəntli]ad. 不变地；不断地；持久的；时常 地 例 We must constantly adjust the amount of currency in circulation.
[08:47.64]affinity [əˈfɪnəti]n. 密切关系；(天生的)喜爱；(相互)吸 引；类同，相像 例 It is clear that there exists an affinity between open politics and open markets.
[09:01.32]preliminary [prɪˈlɪmɪnəri]a. 初步的；开始的；预备的 n. 准 备；预赛；[pl.]初步措施 搭 preliminary examination 初试；预备考试
[09:11.52]supersonic [ˌsuːpəˈsɒnɪk]a. 超声的；超音速的
