[09:31.08]extensive [ɪkˈstensɪv]a. 广阔的；广泛的，全面的；数目众 多的 例 Extensive reading is a good way to enlarge your vision.
[09:41.52]default [ˈdiːfɔːlt]n. 违约，拖欠；弃权；(计算机)预设 (值)；缺省，缺乏 [dɪˈfɔːlt]vi. 不履行义务；拖欠 例 As a result of the following financial crisis, the company did default on its short-term notes. 搭 in default of 缺乏
[10:00.84]commandment [kəˈmɑːndmənt]n. 戒律；命令 例 Think about how important this commandment is to society and nation. 搭 taboos and commandment 清规戒律
[10:14.76]commentator [ˈkɒmənteɪtə(r)]n. 评论员；实况广播员；注释者 例 According to this view, the perfect economics commentator should have been carefully protected from academic economics.
[10:32.40]faction [ˈfækʃn]n. 组织中的小派别；小集团；派系斗争 例 The progressive faction demanded a reserve system and currency supply owned and controlled by the government.
[10:47.76]tackle [ˈtækl]vt. 对付，处理；与…交涉 n. 用具；钓 具；辘轳，滑车(组) 例 We must coordinate better to tackle the world's ongoing financial crisis. 搭 tackle sb. on/over sth. 就某事与某人交涉
