[12:50.28]progressive [prəˈɡresɪv]a. 进步的；先进的；渐进的；(税收) 累进的，递增的 n. 改革论者；进步分子
[12:57.36]synthetic [sɪnˈθetɪk]a. 合成的，人造的；综合性的
[13:01.44]embargo [ɪmˈbɑːɡəʊ]n. 禁止(或限制)贸易令；禁运 vt. 禁 止或限制(贸易)；禁止(船只)出入港口 例 The US abandoned the trade embargo on many countries. 搭 be under embargo 封港中；禁运中 / lay an embargo on 对…实行禁运 / lift the embargo on 对…解禁
[13:21.36]survive [səˈvaɪv]vt. 比…活得长；幸免于 vi. 幸存 例 Despite the uncertainty of the commercial world, some businesses do survive for centuries.
[13:34.80]alter [ˈɔːltə(r)]v. 改变；改动 例 The digital age has brought all of us new and exciting tools that will surely continue to alter the way we learn and work.
[13:49.56]code [kəʊd]n. 法典，法规；规范，准则；代码，密码 例 The Patent Office rejected his application, citing a clause in the patent code which says that life forms are not patentable. 搭 break a code 破解密码
[14:07.56]manipulate [məˈnɪpjuleɪt]vt. 操作；操纵；篡改(或伪造)账 目；巧妙地处理 例 Throughout his career, he has very successfully manipulated the market with the help of media. 搭 manipulate sb. into (doing) sth. 操纵某人做 某事
[14:27.36]end-product [ˌendˈprɒdʌkt]n. 制成品，最终产品
[14:31.56]subsidy [ˈsʌbsədi]n. 津贴，补贴；补助金 搭 subsidy for …的补贴
[14:36.72]bearer [ˈbeərə(r)]n. 持票人；负荷者；搬运工 a. (证券) 不记名的 例 The payer is supposed to be liable to the bearer.
[14:46.44]regulator [ˈreɡjuleɪtə(r)]n. 调整者，管理者；调节器；标准 计时仪 例 The government often plays the role of watchdog and regulator in marketing operations.
[15:00.72]favouritism [ˈfeɪvərɪtɪzəm]n. 偏爱；偏袒；徇私；不公平 例 The U.S. gets middling global rankings on issues like wasteful government spending and favoritism by government officials. 搭 appoint people by favouritism 任人唯亲
